## Token usage

Web Search usage is measured in tokens. A successful API response includes `usage.input_tokens` for the query and `usage.output_tokens` for the returned content. Both count toward the account's Web Search TPM (rolling 60 seconds) and TPD (UTC day) limits. Titles, URLs and response metadata are not metered. Token prices are currently zero.

Read the API's usage values rather than estimating from character counts. Full-text results count after the per-result character cap; longer content can consume more allowance. Check [Plan & usage](https://docs.langsearch.com/limits/api-limits) for the complete rules, including older content representations.

For HTTP 429, inspect `error_type` when present and honor `Retry-After`. `response_exceeds_token_limit` requires reducing `count` or `contents.text.max_characters`; waiting alone will not make the same oversized response fit. The Dashboard shows tokens used today, percentage used and the next 00:00 UTC reset. Minute usage history can lag the live allowance.

New accounts start at 5 RPS. Existing accounts keep their configured RPS. Web Search uses TPM and TPD token limits, with no separate request-per-minute or request-per-day quotas. Check the Dashboard for account limits.
